    "title": "New Co-Responder Unit Launched to Support Commerce City Residents in Mental Health Crises - NewsBreak",
    "text": "16 minutes ago The Commerce City Police Department has started a new Co-Responder Unit (CRU) to help people experiencing mental health crises. The team includes behavioral health clinicians, a case manager, and Crisis Intervention Team officers who respond together to certain 911 calls.\nThe CRU offers on-scene assessment, de-escalation, and connects individuals to appropriate care. The program is designed to reduce involvement with the criminal justice system or emergency rooms and to improve crisis response for community members.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
